<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-3b82f80661ae988c560c4cae3be2acf069f63c041f0e5677b6f7d2afff9ff4c1">
  
    

  
  

          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/20/010" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.20.010 Definitions.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A. City entity</strong> means any bureau, office, program, employee, or contractor of the City.</span></li><li><span><strong>B. City employee </strong>means any individual employed by the City in a position classified under the categories defined in City Code or Administrative Rule HRAR-3.03.</span></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-08f4900252c74ece5405486ba74fd52d6cc59c79130f4bdc189addc40fee1947">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-22a53d1cb908f99eacca40c2c9f3589f090dbbe7651b5102a684c237e8c56c23">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/20/020" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.20.020 Intent.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A. </strong>The City recognizes and values the diverse contributions of all individuals and affirms its commitment to treating all persons with dignity and respect, regardless of race, color, national origin, immigration or refugee status, heritage, culture, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, ability, age, or economic status.</span></li><li><span>City Council, in the interests of public and community safety, and in the lawful exercise of its authority and for the protection of all persons within its jurisdiction, confirms the City's commitment to safeguarding and supporting immigrant and refugee communities through binding municipal law.</span></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-e6f5f71c854d76824bcbfb96b5d2473f2e1d4a6313aa5190133e2e9858ee6bab">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-5d1d5bef7f04b0197ab70b9e92bed5cc977f5bfcd0bf9ad9770c847aba1b3ee4">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/20/030" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.20.030 Policy.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A. </strong>Consistent with state and federal law, the City prohibits the use of City resources to enforce federal immigration law.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong>City facilities, property, moneys, equipment, technology or personnel may not be used for the purpose of investigating, detecting, apprehending, arresting, detaining or holding persons for the purpose of enforcing federal immigration laws.</span></li><li><span><strong>2.</strong>&nbsp;No City entity or law enforcement agency may enter into a formal or informal agreement with a federal immigration authority relating to the detention of a person for the purpose of enforcing federal immigration laws.</span></li><li><span><strong>3. </strong>Except</span><span>when required by state or federal law, no City entity or law enforcement agency may collect, inquire into, or disclose information concerning an individual's immigration or citizenship status, country of birth, or other personal information for the purpose of enforcing federal immigration laws.</span></li><li><span><strong>4. </strong>The prohibitions and requirements set forth in this Chapter do not apply to the following:</span><ol><li><span><strong>a.</strong> When required by court order, or a warrant authorized by a court;</span></li><li><span><strong>b</strong>. When disclosure is required by a judicial subpoena issued as part of a court proceeding or by another compulsory court-issued legal process;</span></li><li><span><strong>c</strong>. When disclosure is required to effect the international extradition to this state and return of a person charged with or convicted of crimes in this state and for whom a warrant of arrest has been issued;</span></li><li><span><strong>d</strong>. To the extent that the information is available to the general public and under the same terms and conditions as it is available to the general public;</span></li><li><span><strong>e</strong>. When the information is necessary to advance an investigation into a violation of state or local criminal law;</span></li><li><span><strong>f</strong>. When the information is submitted to a court of this state, whether orally or in writing, in connection with a proceeding in that court; or</span></li><li><span><strong>g</strong>. When the information is necessary to determine the individual's eligibility for a benefit the individual is seeking.</span></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>B. </strong>All City staff are required to participate in ongoing training on the City's sanctuary policies. The content of this training will align with federal law, state law, and Portland City Code.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong>Training will include, at a minimum:</span><ol><li><span><strong>a.</strong> Sanctuary City Code provisions and City policies;</span></li><li><span><strong>b.</strong> The distinction between administrative warrants and judicial warrants;</span></li><li><span><strong>c.</strong> The difference between and importance of public and nonpublic spaces, including authorized access to City spaces and facilities;</span></li><li><span><strong>d.</strong> Guidance on responding to inquiries or actions by a federal immigration authority, including requests for information regarding City employees or residents and visitors and attempts to access City property or City-sponsored meetings;</span></li><li><span><strong>e.</strong> The process for rapidly contacting the appropriate City official in urgent situations; and</span></li><li><span><strong>f.</strong> Training specific to supervisory responsibilities.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>2.</strong> The training may also include, but is not limited to:</span><ol><li><span><strong>a</strong>. Information on how and where employees can access relevant City resources and additional learning materials;</span></li><li><span><strong>b</strong>. Resources for City employees directly affected by federal immigration authority enforcement action; and</span></li><li><span><strong>c</strong>. Protocols for supervisors on responding if employees are detained, as well as guidance on compassionate leadership and support for employees.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>3.</strong> The training will be reviewed no less than annually and may be reviewed more frequently as necessary. Revisions will incorporate emerging best practices, newly enacted laws, updated protocols, and relevant resources. Updates will be informed by feedback from Employee Resource Group representatives, relevant and representative bureaus, equity and language subject matter experts, labor union representatives, immigration rights organizations, faith leaders, community leaders, nonprofits, educational institutions and additional community partners.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>C. </strong>City-owned and leased spaces and buildings will display visible signage identifying entry requirements for the public and visitors and the specific areas which are public spaces and all areas that are not.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong> Signage will be in accordance with best practices for language access and plain language, and recommendations of Employee Resource Groups, equity and subject matter experts on immigrant affairs and rights.</span></li><li><span><strong>2. </strong>Signage will include companion resources to explain the signage and contain additional resources and contacts. Companion resources will be based on best practices for language access and plain language, Sanctuary City trainings, and content should be in accordance with immigrant rights organization recommendations.</span></li><li><span><strong>3.</strong> Signage policies and resources will be updated regularly and informed by experts, City Attorney advice, Employee Resource Groups and community leaders in language access, equity, immigrant affairs and rights, and additional relevant subject matters.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>D. </strong>Immigrant affairs tracking evaluation and reporting.</span></li><li><span>The City will regularly review their existing programs and services to identify ways to comply with this Code Section, and implement best practices and policies for staff and communities impacted by immigration.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1. </strong>Every City bureau and office will provide the following information to Council at least quarterly:</span><ol><li><span><strong>a</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp; Employee training completion rates;</span></li><li><span><strong>b</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp; Federal enforcement activity on City property and facilities; and</span></li><li><span><strong>c</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp; Known violations of the Sanctuary Promise Act by City employees.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>2. </strong>The City will also provide an annual report to Council summarizing Freedom of Information Act requests, immigration enforcement communication, requests, and activities and a detailed description of the City's response.</span></li><li><span><strong>3. </strong>The City will provide a report at least annually to Council. The report will be combined and coordinated. It will include the following:</span><ol><li><span><strong>a.</strong>&nbsp; An evaluation of training on City's sanctuary policies; and</span></li><li><span><strong>b.</strong>&nbsp; Compliance with City's sanctuary policies; and</span></li><li><span><strong>c.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; Information on sanctuary-related policies and procedures in similar local jurisdictions.</span></li><li><span><strong>d.</strong>&nbsp; Reviewal and evaluation will be informed by feedback from Employee Resource Group representatives, relevant and representative bureaus, equity and language subject matter experts, labor union representatives, immigration rights organizations, faith leaders, community leaders, non-profits, educational institutions and additional community partners.</span></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-c413dc94e5fdfda0c0cf37ec42e8cbf5ddfbb281e8982b873f041f9c3df768b1">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-244110ad83a8f02ddbeca43c20804ff7f3e40d8ddf91e860f067e5967d73d74e">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/20/040" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.20.040 Exceptions.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A. </strong>The prohibitions set forth in this Chapter do not apply to the arrest by Portland Police Bureau of individuals who have been formally charged by the United States with a criminal offense under federal immigration law, as specified in Title II of the Immigration and Nationality Act or under 18 U.S.C. §§ 1015, 1422–1429, or 1505, and who are subject to arrest for the crime pursuant to a judicial warrant of arrest issued by a federal magistrate.</span></li><li><span><strong>B. </strong>The Portland Police Bureau will include in its annual report to the City Council a section that details all instances in which receives communication or request from a federal agency that relates to immigration enforcement, including exception applied in Subsection 23.20.030 A.4 above. The report will include details about the basis for the exception for each instance, including the justification for each instance. Additionally, each instance will be reported with the legally disclosable information for the name and title of the official who authorized the action, a comprehensive description of the action taken, and the identities and roles of any federal agents involved.</span></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-f3a974ebc86c090ae509558483f844778143e19a7f44875a95da67f96c43f59b">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-d3c5e70c32f22304a28734fc2054b6caf167b05f12227a457c5e54f7ff952738">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>
</span></div>
    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
      <div class="views-field views-field-rendered-entity"><span class="field-content">    
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h2>
        <a href="/code/23/30" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">Chapter 23.30 Identiﬁcation of Law Enforcement Oﬃcers</span>
</a>
    </h2>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-prefix-note field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p>(Added by Ordinance 192184, effective June 26, 2026.)</p></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-349e532cafd91c50fca1e55e8a1c0416fc2eeef90fb4176d38d43fc1924ece56">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-6c548b84b6f867d024d58701e23632d03d61aca19af8d4c3ad6cbdf88df7f780">
  
    

  
  

          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/010" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.010 Policy.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p><span>Law enforcement oﬃcers who are easily identiﬁable promote transparency in their duties and strengthen trust between agencies and the communities they serve. An oﬃcer's visible face facilitates communication, allows for the reading of expressions, and helps reduce the risk of conﬂict in emotionally charged situations. Oﬃcers shall maintain professionalism by clearly identifying themselves when engaged in oﬃcial activity, ensuring that their appearance and conduct promote public conﬁdence and safety.Any person arrested in the City of Portland has the right to know the identity of the arresting officer.</span></p><p><span>This Chapter establishes standards for law enforcement oﬃcer identiﬁcation, veriﬁcation of apparent law enforcement activity occurring within the City, and the documentation of people presenting as oﬃcers. The City will comply with this Chapter in a manner consistent with all applicable federal and state laws.</span></p></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-6a66a3a0c48469338aeb56110a0514c715f58cd6a7e55d3426cd5729a559928f">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-494049b26358befb857f3551ecd29ca863c6f1789b3d9a593ea2102c0cfa951c">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/020" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.020 Definitions.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A.</strong>&nbsp; <strong>Oﬃcer</strong> means any sworn law enforcement oﬃcer employed by or operating under the jurisdiction of any government agency, or any person purporting to act under the color of law as a law enforcement officer.</span></li><li><span><strong>B.</strong>&nbsp; <strong>PPB oﬃcer&nbsp;</strong>means any sworn employee of the Portland Police Bureau (PPB) acting within the scope of their oﬃcial duties.</span></li><li><span><strong>C. &nbsp;Proof of identity</strong> means a government-issued identification that includes name and photograph of the carrier and a face free of any covering that inhibits the ability to verify that the person in possession of the identification is the person identified.</span></li><li><span><strong>D.&nbsp; Preliminary investigation</strong> means the gathering or verification of information through lawful means. A preliminary investigation may be conducted through consensual contact and does not constitute a detention or seizure unless supported by reasonable suspicion or other lawful authority.</span></li><li><span><strong>E. Proof of authority</strong> means a person is acting within the scope of lawful authority of their law enforcement agency and shall be established by at least one indicia of authority. The indicia set forth below are illustrative and not exhaustive, and nothing herein precludes consideration of other objective evidence establishing lawful authority:</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong>&nbsp; A uniform clearly and visibly displaying a badge number, name, and agency identification;</span></li><li><span><strong>2.</strong>&nbsp; A judicial warrant establishing their authority;</span></li><li><span><strong>3.</strong>&nbsp; Official credentials or identification establishing an individual's confirmed law enforcement status;</span></li><li><span><strong>4.</strong>&nbsp; An appropriately marked vehicle for the entity that employs the law enforcement officer that is visible to individuals beyond such officer;</span></li><li><span><strong>5.&nbsp; </strong>The presence of other identifiable officers in uniform (defined as 23.30.020 E.1.); or</span></li><li><span><strong>6. </strong>Authority verified through a law enforcement agency or dispatch center.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>F. Facial covering </strong>means any opaque mask, garment, helmet, headgear, balaclava, tactical mask, gaiter, ski mask or other item that conceals or obscures the facial identity of an individual. Facial covering does not include:</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong> A medical-grade mask or respirator, including an N95 medical mask, worn to protect against the transmission of disease or infection;</span></li><li><span><strong>2. </strong>Any mask, helmet, or device, including air purifying respirators, full or half masks or self-contained breathing apparatuses, necessary to protect against exposure to toxins, gas, smoke, flame or extreme or severely inclement weather;</span></li><li><p><span><strong>3.</strong> A motorcycle or bicycle helmet worn while a law enforcement officer is operating a motorcycle, bicycle or other vehicle that requires a helmet for safe operation while in the performance of the officer's duties;</span></p><p><span><strong>4. </strong>A fire helmet worn during an arson investigation;</span></p><p><span><strong>5.</strong> Eyewear necessary to protect the eyes from physical objects or retinal weapons;</span></p><p><span><strong>6. </strong>A translucent face shield or clear mask that does not conceal the wearer's facial identity and is used in compliance with the employing law enforcement agency's policy.</span></p></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>G.&nbsp; Law enforcement activities</strong> means activities involving patrol, investigation, arrest, detention, or other direct enforcement of criminal laws, or of civil laws when enforcement involves detention. Law enforcement activities do not include appearances for testimony, training, or community engagement.</span></li><li><span><strong>H. Credible indicia of authority </strong>means proof of identity plus proof of authority. Proof of identity and authority may be established simultaneously when the government-issued identification possessed by the individual claiming law enforcement authority includes a name and photograph as well as law enforcement agency affiliation, and matches a face free of any covering. Credible indicia of authority may be established voluntarily, may be requested, or may be established by observation.</span></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-a85143ad3736124ad07286da45c964d60e50d886bac20d0e6fc74c536ada5389">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-1e5531f96220ccd1de3d2cc3fbc4022cffe4ab78674e355b07a061569e296eda">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/025" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.025 Exemptions for Certain Official Duties.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><strong>A.</strong> Officers may wear facial coverings when:<ol><li><strong>1.</strong> Engaged in undercover duties in the regular performance of the officer's official duties;</li><li><strong>2. </strong>Assigned to a tactical response team, while actively performing tactical duties, if a facial covering is necessary to protect the officer's face from physical harm while performing such duties; or&nbsp;</li><li><strong>3.</strong> Working in extreme or severely inclement weather, including freezing temperatures, high wind or highly dusty conditions.</li></ol></li><li><strong>B.</strong> For purposes of this Section, <strong>tactical response team</strong> includes:<ol><li><strong>1.</strong> A Special Weapons and Tactics (SWAT) team;</li><li><strong>2.</strong> A hazardous device, bomb or explosive ordnance disposal unit;</li><li><strong>3. </strong>A chemical, biological, radiological, nuclear or explosive (CBRNE) response unit; or</li><li><strong>4.</strong> A tactical K-9 unit assigned to support high-risk warrant service, hostage rescue, armed barricade response or active shooter response.</li></ol></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-0d487eb683059249139b1ba3bad38a3980ec5d91d3dc2ae4957d529bfa3714ef">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-f99845082324e9694b176eb7997c092c4ed1d2b4e70e7d61657528f3f7189b91">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/030" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.030 Standards for Identification.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A</strong>.&nbsp; Compliance with State Law. All requirements of this Section shall be interpreted and applied in a manner consistent with Oregon law governing law enforcement identifiability requirements and the legal protections described in Section 23.30.080 of this Chapter. Officers operating within the City shall comply with this Chapter while on duty and actively engaged in official law enforcement activities.</span></li><li><span><strong>B.</strong>&nbsp; Receipt of identiﬁcation.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong>&nbsp; PPB officers shall receive oﬃcial Portland Police Bureau-issued identiﬁcation (badges, nametags, identiﬁcation cards, business cards, etc.) to be used for oﬃcial business.</span></li><li><span><strong>2.&nbsp; </strong>PPB officers shall ensure they have oﬃcial Portland Police Bureau-issued identiﬁcation and an adequate supply of PPB-issued business cards at all times while on duty.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>C.</strong>&nbsp; Display of identiﬁcation.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong>&nbsp; Oﬃcers shall visibly display their agency-issued badge, and permanent identifying number or nametag (including their last name) on their outermost garment and carry their agency-issued identiﬁcation document, except as outlined in Subsections 23.30.025 A.1. and 23.30.030 E.1.</span></li><li><span><strong>2.&nbsp; </strong>Oﬃcers operating in the City of Portland shall not intentionally conceal or obscure their faces through the use of facial coverings except as permitted under Oregon law and Section 23.30.025.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>D.</strong>&nbsp; Providing identiﬁcation to the public.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong>&nbsp; When practical, safe, and tactically feasible, PPB oﬃcers shall, upon request, identify themselves by name and oﬀer their PPB-issued business card containing their Department of Public Safety Standards and Training (DPSST) number.</span></li><li><span><strong>2.</strong> &nbsp;Any person arrested in the City of Portland has the right to know the identity of the arresting officer. When practical, safe, and tactically feasible, officers will identify themselves to the subject of arrest, holding, or detention.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>E.</strong>&nbsp; Masking and identification exceptions.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong> Plainclothes operations. The requirements of Subsections 23.30.030 B., C., and D.1. do not apply to a law enforcement officer who:</span><ol><li><span><strong>a. &nbsp;</strong>Is engaged in undercover duties as part of the regular performance of the officer's official duties.</span></li><li><span><strong>b. &nbsp;</strong>Is engaged in security or escort details as part of the regular performance of the officer's official duties.</span></li><li><span><strong>c. &nbsp;</strong>Responds to exigent circumstances, if the officer is responding to those circumstances while off duty.</span></li><li><span><strong>d. &nbsp;</strong>Is a detective assigned to and actively engaged in investigative duties, including interviewing victims and witnesses.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>2. &nbsp;</strong>Approval and documentation. When a facial-covering exemption under Subsections 23.30.025 A.2. and 3. is used by a PPB officer, the operational necessity must be documented. Exemptions taken under Subsection 23.30.025 A.2. must follow documentation requirements a-d below. Exemptions taken under Subsection 23.30.025 A.3. must follow documentation requirements Subsections b.-c. below:</span><ol><li><span><strong>a.</strong>&nbsp; The PPB oﬃcer's full name;</span></li><li><span><strong>b.</strong>&nbsp; Assigned duties or deployment at the time of the exception;</span></li><li><span><strong>c.</strong>&nbsp; The speciﬁc rationale for the exception; and</span></li><li><span><strong>d.</strong>&nbsp; The name and rank of the supervising PPB officer who authorized the exception or who was notified and ratified the exception when prior approval was not practicable.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>3.&nbsp; </strong>Facial covering exceptions used by a law enforcement officer shall not be used to impair review of, or accountability for, their official actions.</span></li></ol></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-63d05631d1ac233f22910972d81eaf5745f3c02a8b8b9513e82acd3c23e83e21">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-de6e14157b196aead6b7b60cf8c422156e04d299130dc7bf8b02cc9930f151fe">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/050" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.050 Preliminary Investigations of Potential Impostors.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><p><span><strong>A.</strong>&nbsp; Scope. This Section applies when a person lacking immediate proof of authority is engaged in conduct that would be unlawful for a civilian but would be lawful only if the person were a sworn law enforcement officer acting within the scope of official duties.</span></p><p><span>PPB officers shall make reasonable efforts to determine whether the person is, in fact, a law enforcement officer acting under lawful authority. &nbsp;If such determination cannot immediately be made, an officer will proceed with a preliminary investigation.</span></p><p><span>Verification procedures under this Chapter shall be implemented in a manner consistent with Oregon law.</span></p></li><li><span><strong>B. &nbsp;</strong>Preliminary investigation.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>PPB officers will conduct a preliminary investigation.PPB officers will notify a supervisor and investigate the situation for a potential criminal act. Officers will contact possible agencies or dispatch centers to verify their authority.</span></li><li><span>Preliminary investigations may continue until PPB, based upon the totality of the circumstances, determines whether reasonable suspicion exists to believe the person has committed, is committing, or is about to commit a criminal offense.</span></li><li><span><strong>C.</strong>&nbsp; Investigations with reasonable suspicion. When reasonable suspicion exists based on the totality of circumstances including but not limited to information gathered in the preliminary investigation in Subsection 23.30.050 B., that the person has committed, is committing, or is about to commit a criminal offense, PPB officers will treat the situation as a potential criminal act, as permitted by law and may detain the person.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.</strong>&nbsp; Any commands, restraint, or detention must be limited in scope and duration to what is reasonably necessary to confirm or dispel the officer's reasonable suspicion and to address legitimate safety concerns.</span></li><li><span><strong>2.</strong>&nbsp; PPB officers will, when supported by reasonable suspicion and as permitted by law, issue commands, restrain, or detain the person claiming to be a law enforcement officer to preserve public safety, and investigate the conduct.</span></li><li><span><strong>3.</strong>&nbsp; If it is determined that the person is a law enforcement officer acting within the scope of lawful duties, PPB officers shall promptly end any continued detention or restraint and document the circumstances of the encounter.</span></li></ol></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-376220840b47f9c03f191c2e08520b6faafd3be9e229370ce928ee60395dd99d">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-9a44c10f94af4d13b1c05314c071f36244e2facb8841899df09147ffb1d82d6f">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/060" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.060 Incident Reports.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A.</strong>&nbsp; Scope.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>This Section refers to all police actions and encounters undertaken as outlined in Section 23.30.050.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.&nbsp; </strong>Incident reporting and documentation. All police actions and encounters will be documented in writing including the time and location of the incident; what instigated police involvement; indicia of authority observed or absent; steps taken to verify law enforcement authority; and the outcome.</span></li><li><span>The written report will also include whether the conduct is determined to be criminal, and any relevant police report number. The written report will include, if known, the investigated law enforcement officer's name, badge number, and agency. If the PPB officer observed that the person in question was wearing a mask, or was not wearing a badge, or was not wearing either a permanent identifying number or a name tag, the report shall include that information.</span></li><li><span><strong>2.</strong> Body-worn camera.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Where possible, encounters should be recorded on body-worn camera to the extent allowed by law and in accordance with Portland Police Bureau body-worn camera policy.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Body-worn camera footage under this Section will be retained by the City for the maximum period allowed by law.</span></li></ol></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-c55c73bff16ca59d2bcfe47a16a81f07d423afd81147f9f727cd5265bbce4c8e">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-1f9b94e2ce7a65e68ed85e4973b30f0ff4d7b307aa7df9d6f852ee8b71e7c779">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/070" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.070 Compliance and Reporting.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A.</strong> The Portland Police Bureau will include in its Annual Report to the City Council details of compliance with this Chapter. The report will include a summary of the number and nature of mask exemptions. The report will also include all veriﬁcation incidents in Section 23.30.050,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>the external law enforcement agencies with which authority was veriﬁed, and the outcomes.</span></li><li><span><strong>B.</strong>The Portland Police Bureau shall inform interagency partners known to be operating in the City of the standards established by state law and this Chapter.</span></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-eb051242f96e1872a8a59c50b701dbbf70f807621f42baa8d68a82615323e73f">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-fbb3b5e3e6feea943cf695be784af6ea02e0b963f2cdee490f43ec88daf0ed60">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/080" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.080 Legal Protections.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p><span>Nothing in this Chapter shall be construed to supersede, limit, or otherwise diminish any rights, protections, or regulatory requirements established under federal law, or under the Americans with Disabilities Act or occupational-safety regulations. Oﬃcers shall comply with this Chapter in a manner consistent with all applicable state and federal laws. The City will comply with any bargaining obligations as required under the Public Employees Collective Bargaining Act (PECBA).</span></p></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-e897e9fd9c92713a268505c44e01dae76485a642844b5d23a9849e62a52b7d8c">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-f253eaf508d5efe866a1605e4f3d9113e1ce22890a3a7a88f5615be57a523833">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/090" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.090 Severability of Provisions.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p><span>If any part or provision of this Chapter, or application thereof to any person or circumstance, is held invalid, the remainder of this Chapter and the application of the provision or part thereof to other persons not similarly situated or to other circumstances will not be affected by it and will continue in full force and effect. To this end, provisions of this Chapter are severable.</span></p></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-1658482c2b88e0ea84c955637e47a78f13dbf43dad735c497d269edad69c56c1">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-aa8e9efa32853e459324a07612081cb1ecada0cb1ddeb5a3bac39ccfabede2a9">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/23/30/100" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">23.30.100 Enforcement.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p><span>A violation of this Chapter does not constitute a criminal offense and is not subject to the general penalty provisions of Portland City Code Section 1.01.110.</span></p><p><span>This Chapter regulates the conduct of law enforcement officers and agencies while performing official duties and shall be implemented through administrative, supervisory, employment, or civil processes authorized by law.</span></p><p><span>The Mayor or Council by resolution may authorize the City of Portland to bring a lawsuit seeking injunctive relief requiring officers of an agency to abide by the masking and identification standards of this Chapter that apply to such officers.</span></p></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-6dab42e50e57a0e570e14ddec588252891d50a390b89bb6919fade5cfa4a5778">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-56a56591656c392a8de13c8dc6dd46901e4d9a3147bd34f9805734fbf6fc916a">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>
</span></div>
    </div>
  
    </div>
  
          </div>
</div>

    </div>
  </div>

    </div>
  
